==English==
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɔːkɒn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-walk-on.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[student]] [[athlete]] who wants to [[try out]] for a [[college]] [[sports]] or [[athletic]] [[team]] without the [[benefit]] of a [[scholarship]] or having been [[recruited]].
# {{lb|en|theatre|film}} An [[actor]] of a small (or "[[bit part|bit]]") part in a [[theatrical]] [[production]] or [[film]], often without speaking lines.
# {{lb|en|mostly|attributive}} Such a part in a [[play]] or film.
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1975|author=w:David Gilmour; w:Roger Waters|title={{w|Wish You Were Here (Pink Floyd song)|Wish You Were Here}}|artist=w:Pink Floyd|album={{w|Wish You Were Here (Pink Floyd album)|Wish You Were Here}}|passage=Did you exchange / A '''walk-on''' part in the war for a lead role in a cage?}}
# One who arrives and boards transport (such as a train or ferry) without having booked in advance.

